urity's trading currency, brought to the EPS unit) divided by Bloomberg's adjusted (comparable) earnings per share (IS_COMP_EPS_ADJUSTED), joined on fiscal_year; the median over the closed fiscal years carrying both with adjusted EPS above zero."}}}, "px_last": {"value": 1503.2, "mnemonic": "PX_LAST", "vintage": "2026-09-30T08:39:21Z"}, "ratio_to_px_last": 0.8979037624716334, "band": [0.33, 3.0], "band_basis": {"low": {"value": 0.33, "calibration": "uncalibrated", "basis": "AMGT_CORPUS round 6 h-2 @6d18367755: the 0.33-0.5 bin is EMPTY over 97 measured block keys and the only name below 0.33 is refused for a different cause, so this floor has never decided a case in the measured population."}, "high": {"value": 3.0, "calibration": "measured", "basis": "AMGT_CORPUS round 6 h-2 @6d18367755: over 97 measured block keys two names sit inside the ceiling between 2.5 and 3.0 and one sits just outside at 3.043, so this ceiling discriminates real cases."}}, "label": "Opal's historical-multiple reference", "formula_words": "Bloomberg consensus EPS (FY1) x adjusted trailing-median P/E"}, "upside": {"status": "ABSENT", "reason": "methodology to be discussed with Andrew"}, "downside": {"status": "ABSENT", "reason": "methodology to be discussed with Andrew"}}, "reason": null, "generated_at": "2026-09-30T11:36Z", "team_cases": {"base": {"status": "SERVED", "table": {"EPS": {"2026E": "31.59", "2027E": "41.44", "2028E": "47.67", "2029E": "56.94", "2030E": "61.42"}, "Multiple": {"2026E": "30.0x", "2027E": "30.0x", "2028E": "30.0x", "2029E": "30.0x", "2030E": "30.0x"}, "Price": {"2026E": "948", "2027E": "1,243", "2028E": "1,430", "2029E": "1,708", "2030E": "1,843"}, "Return": {"2026E": "-22.5%", "2027E": "1.7%", "2028E": "17.0%", "2029E": "39.8%", "2030E": "50.7%"}}, "citation": {"locator": 0, "passage": "2026E 2027E 2028E 2029E 2030E | EPS 31.59 41.44 47.67 56.94 61.42 | Multiple 30.0x 30.0x 30.0x 30.0x 30.0x | Price 948 1,243 1,430 1,708 1,843 | Return -22.5% 1.7% 17.0% 39.8% 50.7%", "report_id": "37aa7a78aca3d4fc", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ASML_NA_Equity/37aa7a78aca3d4fc/ASML research pack 5_5_2026.pdf"}, "currency": null, "currency_basis": "not stated in the pack", "unit_as_written": null}, "upside": {"status": "SERVED", "table": {"EPS": {"2026E": "31.02", "2027E": "37.78", "2028E": "46.12", "2029E": "55.23", "2030E": "67.11"}, "Multiple": {"2026E": "34.0x", "2027E": "34.0x", "2028E": "34.0x", "2029E": "34.0x", "2030E": "34.0x"}, "Price": {"2026E": "1,055", "2027E": "1,284", "2028E": "1,568", "2029E": "1,878", "2030E": "2,282"}, "Return": {"2026E": "-13.7%", "2027E": "5.1%", "2028E": "28.3%", "2029E": "53.6%", "2030E": "86.7%"}}, "citation": {"locator": 0, "passage": "2026E 2027E 2028E 2029E 2030E | EPS 31.02 37.78 46.12 55.23 67.11 | Multiple 34.0x 34.0x 34.0x 34.0x 34.0x | Price 1,055 1,284 1,568 1,878 2,282 | Return -13.7% 5.1% 28.3% 53.6% 86.7%", "report_id": "37aa7a78aca3d4fc", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ASML_NA_Equity/37aa7a78aca3d4fc/ASML research pack 5_5_2026.pdf"}, "currency": null, "currency_basis": "not stated in the pack", "unit_as_written": null}, "downside": {"status": "SERVED", "table": {"EPS": {"2026E": "27.26", "2027E": "29.48", "2028E": "32.05", "2029E": "34.26", "2030E": "37.25"}, "Multiple": {"2026E": "24.0x", "2027E": "24.0x", "2028E": "24.0x", "2029E": "24.0x", "2030E": "24.0x"}, "Price": {"2026E": "654", "2027E": "707", "2028E": "769", "2029E": "822", "2030E": "894"}, "Return": {"2026E": "-46.5%", "2027E": "-42.1%", "2028E": "-37.1%", "2029E": "-32.7%", "2030E": "-26.9%"}}, "citation": {"locator": 0, "passage": "2026E 2027E 2028E 2029E 2030E | EPS 27.26 29.48 32.05 34.26 37.25 | Multiple 24.0x 24.0x 24.0x 24.0x 24.0x | Price 654 707 769 822 894 | Return -46.5% -42.1% -37.1% -32.7% -26.9%", "report_id": "37aa7a78aca3d4fc", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ASML_NA_Equity/37aa7a78aca3d4fc/ASML research pack 5_5_2026.pdf"}, "currency": null, "currency_basis": "not stated in the pack", "unit_as_written": null}}, "line_names": {"PX_LAST": "Share price (last close)", "SALES_REV_TURN": "Revenue", "IS_OPER_INC": "Operating income", "OPER_MARGIN": "Operating margin", "CAPITAL_EXPEND": "Capital expenditure", "CF_FREE_CASH_FLOW": "Free cash flow", "CURRENT_EV_TO_T12M_EBITDA": "Enterprise value to trailing EBITDA", "REVENUE_PER_SH": "Revenue per share", "FREE_CASH_FLOW_YIELD": "Free cash flow yield", "FREE_CASH_FLOW_MARGIN": "Free cash flow margin", "PROF_MARGIN": "Net profit margin", "BS_CASH_NEAR_CASH_ITEM": "Cash and near-cash items", "BS_TOTAL_LIABILITIES": "Total liabilities", "IS_ADJUSTED_GROSS_PROFIT": "Adjusted gross profit", "IS_ADJUSTED_OPERATING_INCOME": "Adjusted operating income", "IS_COMP_EPS_ADJUSTED": "Adjusted earnings per share", "NET_INCOME": "Net income", "EQY_DPS": "Dividend per share, alternate definition", "IS_DIL_EPS_CONT_OPS": "Diluted EPS, continuing operations", "PX_TO_FREE_CASH_FLOW": "Price to free cash flow", "GROSS_MARGIN": "Gross margin", "EBITDA_TO_REVENUE": "EBITDA as a share of revenue", "RETURN_ON_CAP": "Return on capital", "RETURN_ON_INV_CAPITAL": "Return on invested capital", "RETURN_ON_TANGIBLE_ASSETS": "Return on tangible assets"}}, "dossier_fields": {"thesis_pillars": [{"citation": {"extract_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report-extract/security_key=ASML_NA_Equity/37aa7a78aca3d4fc/extract.json", "locator": 2, "passage": "ng margin 35% \nand growing, solid free cash flow (margin 34%) and net cash on the balance sheet. \n \nSecular growth tailwinds trump short-term cyclicality in this trillion dollar market: \nChips are the building blocks for the digital economy. They are pervasive, powering \neverything f", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ASML_NA_Equity/37aa7a78aca3d4fc/ASML research pack 5_5_2026.pdf"}, "pillar": "Secular growth tailwinds trump short-term cyclicality in this trillion dollar market", "terms": ["Secular growth tailwinds trump short-term cyclicality in this trillion dollar market"], "text": "Chips are the building blocks for the digital economy. They are pervasive, powering everything from smartphones and computers to datacenters, cars and medical devices. Global semiconductor sales have grown mid-single-digits annually for decades to $800bn in 2025, expected to top $1tn this year. Wafer fabrication equipment sales (including lithography machines) have grown high-single-digits annually since the late 1980s, with acceleration in recent years (5-year CAGR is 15.8%). WFE is high-teens as a percent of global semi sales (and growing), and lithography represents 25-30% of total WFE spend (and growing)."}, {"citation": {"extract_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report-extract/security_key=ASML_NA_Equity/37aa7a78aca3d4fc/extract.json", "locator": 2, "passage": "l semi sales (and growing), and \nlithography represents 25-30% of total WFE spend (and growing). \n \nMonopoly in EUV lithography with an impregnable moat: ASML dominates its part \nof the value chain, with 90% of the DUV lithography market and 100% of EU", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ASML_NA_Equity/37aa7a78aca3d4fc/ASML research pack 5_5_2026.pdf"}, "pillar": "Monopoly in EUV lithography with an impregnable moat", "terms": ["Monopoly in EUV lithography with an impregnable moat"], "text": "ASML dominates its part of the value chain, with 90% of the DUV lithography market and 100% of EUV. The other two competitors in DUV are Nikon and Canon. ASML benefits from a system of interlocking barriers that make its position nearly impossible to replicate. Their technology is the embodiment of accumulated engineering knowledge across hundreds of interdependent subsystems (laser physics, vacuum engineering, mirror optics, etc.) which took decades of effort and significant resources to master. Switching costs are high (in time in and in money) as they co-develop technology roadmaps with customers who have each invested billions into integration. The services component deepens their already entrenched customer relationships."}], "management": {"status": "SERVED", "value": "Management and capital allocation: President and CEO Christophe Fouquet joined ASML in 2008 and held several management positions in marketing and product management prior to CEO, including Chief Business Officer from 2022 to 2024, EVP of EUV from 2018 to 2022 and EVP of Applications from 2013 to 2018. Prior to ASML, he worked at industry peers KLA Tencor and Applied Materials. Executives are long-tenured with decades of accumulated technical knowledge. While CFO Roger Dassen comes from a pure finance and audit background (previously at Deloitte), there are mostly engineers at the top (the CEO has a physics background, and the CTO is a mathematician). On capital allocation, the hierarchy follows a fairly classic framework for a capital-light, high-margin industrial business. Priorities include 1) reinvesting back into the business, with R&D treated as sacrosanct and cap ex spend to scale production capacity, and 2) returning excess capital to shareholders through dividends and share buybacks. Over the last three decades, they\u2019ve spent nearly \u20ac34bn on a cumulative basis on R&D, which is consistently low- to mid-teens as a percent of total sales. This spend is not discretionary, but rather the engine that sustains the monopoly. Since the mid-1990s, ASML has spent nearly \u20ac15bn on cap ex on a cumulative basis (typically mid- to high-single-digits as a percent of sales) to ensure sufficient manufacturing capacity to build enough machines to meet demand. ASML has returned \u20ac16.7bn in dividends over the last two decades, and they\u2019ve repurchased \u20ac28.2bn in stock over that same time frame. Nearly 75% of buybacks have occurred in the last five years. While M&A is not a priority, ASML has made selective, strategic acquisitions over time, mostly to internalize critical technology dependencies (for example, acquiring Cymer for their industry leading laser light sources).", "citation": {"locator": 3, "passage": "Management and capital allocation: President and CEO Christophe Fouquet joined ASML in 2008 and held several management positions in marketing and product management prior to CEO, including Chief Business Officer from 2022 to 2024, EVP of EUV from 2018 to 2022 and EVP of Applications from 2013 to 20", "report_id": "37aa7a78aca3d4fc", "report_key": "s3://opal-data-harvest/amgt/harvest/bronze/research-report/security_key=ASML_NA_Equity/37aa7a78aca3d4fc/ASML research pack 5_5_2026.pdf"}}, "fund_of_record": {"status": "ABSENT", "value": null, "reason": "no report's RECOMMENDATION line names a fund token (IDVZ|PFOE|DIVZ)"}, "last_stated_position": {"status": "ABSENT", "value": null, "reason": "no report carries a non-empty RECOMMENDATION line"}}, "generated_at": "2026-09-30T11:36Z", "drafted_sections": [{"section_id": "company_description", "label": "Company description", "sentences": [{"text": "Board holdings: members of ASML's current Board of Management and Supervisory Board (8 persons) held 51,095.11 shares, or 0.01%.", "generated": true, "evidence": [{"id": "P0064", "passage": "Members of ASML's current Board of Management and Supervisory Board (8 persons) 3", "source": {"accession": "000162828026011378", "document_sha256": "865382553cf9871c78bcf144818b6e2d425af3bdc3013ab6c1bf83c85d8ed358", "excerpt_sha256": "e28dd343361e86e59b4a565f4416b0259ebaf28f5a529cc365934c7e45b44abb", "location": "ITEM 3.D. RISK FACTORS / 5.09% / paragraph 65"}}, {"id": "P0065", "passage": "1. Based solely on the Schedule 13-G/A filed by Blackrock, Inc. with the SEC on April 23, 2025, BlackRock, Inc reports voting power with respect", "source": {"accession": "000162828026011378", "document_sha256": "865382553cf9871c78bcf144818b6e2d425af3bdc3013ab6c1bf83c85d8ed358", "excerpt_sha256": "e28dd343361e86e59b4a565f4416b0259ebaf28f5a529cc365934c7e45b44abb", "location": "ITEM 3.D. RISK FACTORS / 0.01% / paragraph 66"}}], "verbatim_check": "PASS", "quoted_spans": ["members of ASML's current Board of Management and Supervisory Board (8 persons)"]}], "held_no_span_at_read": 5, "description_verdict_state": "FAILED", "description_verdict_reason": "no served D-1 company_description sentence passing the describes-the-business test"}, {"section_id": "investment_thesis", "label": "Investment thesis", "sentences": [], "held_no_span_at_read": 1}, {"section_id": "risks", "label": "Risks", "sentences": [], "held_no_span_at_read": 2}, {"section_id": "ceo_bio", "label": "CEO bio", "sentences": [], "held_no_span_at_read": 0, "absent": {"reason": "the officer roster and the role-start field are not extracted at this cut; the filing's officer section is PERSISTED on the source object and its extraction is AMGT-rj-8's", "owner": "AMGT-rj-8"}}, {"section_id": "recommendation", "label": "Recommendation", "sentences": [{"text": "The updated Dutch Corporate Governance Code 2025 applies to financial years starting on or after January 1, 2025, and to comply ASML has included a Risk Management Statement in its 2025 Annual Report based on EU-IFRS.", "generated": true, "evidence": [{"id": "P0002", "passage": "to the financial years starting on or after January 1, 2025,", "source": {"accession": "000162828026011378", "document_sha256": "865382553cf9871c78bcf144818b6e2d425af3bdc3013ab6c1bf83c85d8ed358", "excerpt_sha256": "e28dd343361e86e59b4a565f4416b0259ebaf28f5a529cc365934c7e45b44abb", "location": "ITEM 3.D. RISK FACTORS / Governance Code 2025 was published, which applies / paragraph 3"}}], "verbatim_check": "PASS", "quoted_spans": ["financial years starting on or after January 1, 2025,"]}], "held_no_span_at_read": 0}], "drafting_status": "SERVED", "drafting_source": "pool", "